The current tools resolve two closeout gaps: jobq excludes GPU jobs from builds, and abrun checks flags and switch activation before scoring. I’ll document those procedures and distinguish tested behavior from untested code and superseded scripts. The over-memory wrapper also differs from its header: its effective watchdog defaults are 600 MiB available memory, 2560 MiB swap used, and 1000 MiB/s swap traffic.
